-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/7e00c3bb-fb4c-56c7-97b3-c4a7c3e06f8f
-- title:
--   Supersingular DVR, Drinfeld chart, nodes and inertia at q=2
-- statement:
--   **Setting.** Fix a prime $q$ together with the hypothesis `hq2 : q = 2`, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and an auxiliary prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$, and write $\kappa$ for its residue field.
--
--   *Supersingular places.* `W` is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa$-Laurent series generated by the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of $j(M'\tau)$) over $\kappa$, and `hW` says that its members are exactly the elements of `ssPlaces q M' κ`: the places $w$ that are rational (the map $\kappa \to$ residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M' w`, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the geometric generator `jGeomGen κ M'` in the set `ssJSet q κ`. A place $s \in W$ is fixed.
--
--   *Function fields.* `hle` asserts `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`, where the former is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, and the latter is the analogous base change of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ with $H = \ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\big)$.
--
--   *Constant reduction.* `R₀` is a `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, and the compatibilities with $A$ on constants recorded in that structure. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the element lies in `R₀.integers` and its `R₀`-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *Small-field data.* `k₀` is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$; the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` say that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, and `hκ` says that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   *Roots of unity and tame uniformiser.* $\ell$ is a prime with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; $\varpi_t \in k_0$ has image in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *Base layer.* `Kb` is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with `hKb : Kb = ⊥` (so `Kb` is $k_0$ itself), `Ab` is the valuation subring of `Kb` cut out by $A$, and $\varpi_b \ne 0$ generates the maximal ideal of `Ab`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** With `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $F_0$ be any intermediate field of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ characterised by the coefficient condition: $f \in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in (the image of) $k_0$. Then there exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (1) $W_0$ meets $k_0$ in $A$: for $x \in k_0$ one has $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, and (3) the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal.
--
--   (4) *Specialisation at $s$.* For every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ whose base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `R₀.integers`, such that $g$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which $j$ has non-negative order, and whose `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with image in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the `R₀`-residue of $g$, the difference of the image of $g$ and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) *Level stability.* For every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subset \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and every $f \in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` again in $F_0$: $f \in W_0$ if and only if `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in W_0$.
--
--   (6) *Affine chart.* There exist a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an `Ab`-algebra structure on $B$ such that:
--
--   (6a) the structure map sends $a \in$ `Ab` to the image of $a \in$ `Kb` $\subset \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in `fieldBar q M'`;
--
--   (6b) $B$ is contained in the compositum of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of `Kb` with $F_0$, and (6c) every element of that compositum is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \ne 0$;
--
--   (6d) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over `Ab`, and (6e) $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (6f) every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; (6g) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime; (6h) $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at that prime: $f \in W_0$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$;
--
--   (6i) the image of the $q$-expansion of $j$ lies in $B$, and (6j) $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for all $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (6k) there exists $b \in F_0 \cap B$ such that $b \notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which meets $k_0$ in $A$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains the image of $j$, and is such that $p(j)$ is a unit of $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$;
--
--   (6l) for every $s' \in W$ with $s' \ne s$ there exists $b \in F_0 \cap B$ such that $b \notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which meets $k_0$ in $A$ and satisfies the specialisation property (4) with $s$ replaced by $s'$;
--
--   (6m) *Drinfeld identification.* For every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to the fixed field [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) inside the Drinfeld function field such that: $\#C_s =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` (for $q = 2$ this is $12$ or $1$ according as $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen` vanishes or not, divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`); $\ker \rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ composed with the structure map of `Ab` is the reduction $A \to \kappa$ followed by the structure map; every element of the target is a quotient of two $\rho$-values; the range of $\rho$ consists exactly of the elements whose image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21); and for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), and $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` in $B$, the $\rho$-image of the latter is the value of [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at that group element on $\rho(f)$;
--
--   (6n) *Drinfeld identification with tame inertia.* For every ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb{F}_{q^2} \to \kappa$, with the induced algebra structure, and every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, there is a subgroup $C_s$ with $\#C_s =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` such that for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` there is $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with the kernel, `Ab`-compatibility, quotient-surjectivity, range and $\Gamma_0(M')$-equivariance properties as in (6m), and in addition: there is $\eta \in \{1, q\}$ such that for every $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$, every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` preserving $k_0$, every $\alpha \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $\iota(\alpha) =$ `A.tameCharacter π τ`, and every semilinear automorphism $g$ of `fieldBar q M'` equal to [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) of the level-$q^2M'$ field at $\tau$: the subring $B$ is $g$-stable, and for every $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ whose image in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ equals $\alpha^{q+1}$, with $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^\eta)^{-1}, \alpha^\eta)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), and every $f \in B$ with $g \cdot f \in B$, the $\rho$-image of $g\cdot f$ is the value of [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at that group element on $\rho(f)$;
--
--   (6o) *Nodes.* There exist: a witness that the base change of the $q$-expansion of $j$ lies in `R₀.integers`; a witness that its `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$; a witness `hJK` that `jqNModC Qbar q` (the $q$-expansion of $j(q\tau)$) lies in `fieldBar q M'`; an element $a_0 \in k_0$ with image in $A$ whose residue satisfies $\mathrm{res}(a_0)^q = s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the `R₀`-residue of $j$; and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ such that:
--
--   — `nodes` has exactly $q+1$ elements;
--
--   — there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$, generated as a ring by the images of the elements of $k_0$ lying in $A$ together with a finite set $T$, with $B_c \subseteq O$ for every $O \in$ `nodes`, and each such $O$ is the localisation of $B_c$ in the sense that $f \in O$ if and only if $f\,h = g$ for some $g, h \in B_c$ with $h$ a unit of $O$;
--
--   — the level automorphisms permute the nodes: for each $\zeta$, each $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and each $O \in$ `nodes` there is $O' \in$ `nodes` with $f \in O \iff$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in O'$ (for $f \in F_0$ with image again in $F_0$); and the action is transitive: for each $\zeta$ and each pair $O, O' \in$ `nodes` there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ realising such an equivalence;
--
--   — distinct nodes are separated: for $O \ne O'$ in `nodes` there is $f$ lying in both which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$;
--
--   — *domination.* Every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ meeting $k_0$ in $A$ and satisfying the specialisation property (4) at $s$ either contains $B$, or dominates some $O \in$ `nodes`, in the sense that $O \subseteq V$ and every non-unit of $O$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$;
--
--   — for each $O \in$ `nodes`: $O \subseteq W_0$; $O$ is a Noetherian local ring; $O$ meets $k_0$ in $A$; every $f \in O$ is congruent to a constant, i.e. there is $x \in k_0$ with image in $A$ and in $O$ such that $f - x$ is a non-unit of $O$; and there exist $E_0 \ge 1$ with the following data. First, a witness that $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,w}\,v$ where $w =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` and $v \in k_0$ has both $v$ and $v^{-1}$ in $A$. Second, a witness that $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota_O$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion $\widehat{A \cap k_0}$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$ (two-variable power series modulo $UV - \pi_0^{E_0}$), and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that model, such that: $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$; $\iota_O$ carries the images of the elements of $k_0 \cap A$ to the corresponding constants of the model; $\iota_O(c_x) = \gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota_O(c_y) = \gamma_V\,V$; $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, whereas $c_x$, if in $W_0$, is not in the maximal ideal. Third, a Hasse-type expansion at the node: witnesses that `jqNModC Qbar q` minus the image of $a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$, an integer $e \ge 1$ and a unit $w_V$ of the model with $\iota_O$ of that element equal to $w_V\,V^{e}$. Fourth, a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ with: $O \subseteq W_x$; $W_x$ meets $k_0$ in $A$; $W_x$ a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; an element $t \in W_x$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then all coefficients of $p$ do; $c_x$ in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ not; for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ field whose base change lies in `R₀.integers` and which has non-negative order wherever $j$ does, the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ exactly when its `R₀`-residue vanishes, and, if its `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $O$ and, for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ with image in $O$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, the difference is a non-unit of $O$; and for every other node $O' \ne O$ there is $f \in O'$ with $f \notin W_x$. Fifth, a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ with: every element of $B_x$ lies in $B$ and in $O$; every element of $B_x$ has non-negative order at each place of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which the image of $j$ has non-negative order; $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ (that is, $f \in O$ iff $f h = g$ with $g, h \in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$); every element of $F_0$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in B_x$, $h \ne 0$; $B_x$ is generated as a ring by the images of the elements of $k_0$ lying in $A$ together with a finite set; and there is $b \in B_x$ such that $b \notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which meets $k_0$ in $A$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains the image of $j$ with $p(j)$ a unit of $V$ for all monic $p$ over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$, and fails to contain some element of $O$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case, worked at an auxiliary rigidifying level divisible by a prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, of the local description of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ above a supersingular point of the level-$M'$ curve in characteristic $q$: a discrete valuation ring on the level field $F_0$ of $q$-expansions with coefficients in $k_0$, an affine chart whose special fibre is identified with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve compatibly with $\Gamma_0(M')$ and with tame inertia, and the $q+1$ node local rings with their crossing-model normal forms. It feeds the downstream packaging statements [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart), [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_nodes_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_nodes_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_nodes_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_nodes_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
